---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research — Paulina Cywoniuk"
  description="Master's thesis research on UI design in VR narrative games. Findings, design tips, and downloadable papers."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="research-hero">
    <p class="research-eyebrow">Master's Thesis · 2026</p>
    <h1 class="research-title">
      How does the design of <em>interaction markers</em> in VR shape players' immersion in a story?
    </h1>
    <p class="research-lede">
      A study of UI design in narrative-driven Virtual Reality —
      and what 35 players taught us about the
      <span class="hl">unexpected</span> ways interfaces shape immersion.
    </p>
    <div class="research-meta">
      <span><strong>Breda University of Applied Sciences</strong></span>
      <span>·</span>
      <span>MSc Game Technology</span>
      <span>·</span>
      <span>2026</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER -->
  <section class="research-figure">
    <div class="figure-placeholder">
      <p>[ Hero image: Echoes of Abandonment — clay-sculpted bedroom ]</p>
      <p class="figure-caption">Drop your game screenshot here once available</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTEXT -->
  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>The question</h2>
    <p>
      VR is becoming a serious medium for storytelling — but the design of its interfaces
      hasn't caught up. Most UI conventions come from flat-screen games:
      menus, button prompts, 2D overlays. These break the very immersion that makes VR worth using.
    </p>
    <p>
      In VR, <strong>the world itself can be the interface</strong>. The objects players touch,
      pick up, and interact with become UI elements. But how do you signal which objects
      are interactive — without breaking the spell?
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STUDY -->
  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>The study</h2>
    <div class="study-stats">
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-number">35</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Participants</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-number">3</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Conditions</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-number">2</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Validated questionnaires</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      I tested three types of interaction markers in
      <em>Echoes of Abandonment</em>, a hand-sculpted VR experience about a child
      coping with their parents' divorce: <strong>diegetic markers</strong> (subtle,
      world-integrated cues), <strong>non-diegetic markers</strong> (overlay icons),
      and a <strong>control group</strong> with no markers. Narrative immersion was
      measured using the IEQ-SF and NES questionnaires alongside custom questions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- FINDINGS -->
  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Key findings</h2>

    <div class="finding-card finding-null">
      <div class="finding-tag">Primary finding</div>
      <h3>Marker design did not significantly affect narrative immersion.</h3>
      <p>
        Statistical analysis (ANOVA, Kruskal-Wallis) showed no significant difference
        between conditions. This null result aligns with prior VR studies —
        but it's only part of the story.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="finding-card finding-surprise">
      <div class="finding-tag">Unexpected finding</div>
      <h3>Non-diegetic markers were more recognisable — and didn't disturb immersion.</h3>
      <p>
        Contrary to my hypothesis, players in the non-diegetic condition reported
        higher recognition of interactable objects without a corresponding drop
        in narrative engagement. This challenges a common assumption in VR design.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="finding-card finding-surprise">
      <div class="finding-tag">Unexpected finding</div>
      <h3>Sound design influenced immersion more than visual UI.</h3>
      <p>
        Multiple participants across conditions cited the game's audio
        (rather than markers) as the immersion-breaking element —
        suggesting that <strong>auditory UI deserves the same scrutiny as visual UI</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TIPS PREVIEW -->
  <section class="research-section tips-preview">
    <h2>Design tips for VR developers</h2>
    <p>
      The most actionable output of this research: a growing library of
      evidence-based design tips for VR developers working with diegetic
      and non-diegetic UI in narrative experiences.
    </p>
    <a href={`/research/tips`.replace('//', '/')} class="btn btn-primary">Browse the tips library →</a>
    <p class="tips-coming-soon">[ Tips library coming soon — currently being built ]</p>
  </section>

  <!-- DOWNLOADS -->
  <section class="research-section downloads">
    <h2>Download the paper</h2>
    <p>The thesis is available in multiple formats depending on how deep you want to go.</p>
    <div class="downloads-grid">
      <a href="#" class="download-card">
        <span class="download-format">1-pager</span>
        <span class="download-desc">The TL;DR — for sharing.</span>
        <span class="download-status">Coming soon</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#" class="download-card">
        <span class="download-format">3-pager</span>
        <span class="download-desc">For practitioners.</span>
        <span class="download-status">Coming soon</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#" class="download-card">
        <span class="download-format">8-page extended abstract</span>
        <span class="download-desc">For conference submission.</span>
        <span class="download-status">Coming soon</span>
      </a>
      <a href="#" class="download-card download-card-primary">
        <span class="download-format">Full thesis (PDF)</span>
        <span class="download-desc">Complete research with methodology and appendices.</span>
        <span class="download-status">Coming soon</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Shared section spacing */
  .research-hero,
  .research-figure,
  .research-section {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem var(--space-page);
  }

  /* HERO */
  .research-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem);
  }

  .research-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-blue);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .research-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .research-title em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-purple);
  }

  .research-lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 55ch;
  }

  .research-lede .hl {
    background-color: var(--color-lime);
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding: 0 0.2em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .research-meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* FIGURE */
  .figure-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    background-color: var(--color-cyan);
    border-radius: 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-purple);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .figure-caption {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* SECTIONS */
  .research-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--color-purple);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .research-section p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .research-section strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* STUDY STATS */
  .study-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-cyan);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .stat {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .stat-number {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--color-purple);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  /* FINDING CARDS */
  .finding-card {
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .finding-null {
    background-color: var(--color-cyan);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-blue);
  }

  .finding-surprise {
    background-color: rgba(199, 239, 0, 0.2);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-lime);
  }

  .finding-tag {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .finding-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--color-purple);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .finding-card p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* TIPS PREVIEW */
  .tips-preview {
    background-color: var(--color-cyan);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .tips-coming-soon {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* DOWNLOADS */
  .downloads-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .download-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, background-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .download-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    background-color: var(--color-lime);
  }

  .download-card-primary {
    background-color: var(--color-purple);
    color: white;
    border-color: var(--color-purple);
  }

  .download-card-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-blue);
    border-color: var(--color-blue);
    color: white;
  }

  .download-format {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .download-desc {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .download-status {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    opacity: 0.6;
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  /* BUTTONS */
  .btn {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, background-color 0.2s ease;
    display: inline-block;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .btn-primary {
    background-color: var(--color-purple);
    color: white;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-blue);
    color: white;
  }
</style>